{
  "id": "p1-component",
  "term": "P1 component",
  "definition": "The P1 component is a feature of the cortical auditory evoked potential used as a marker of auditory cortical maturation. In children with auditory neuropathy spectrum disorder who receive cochlear implants, its presence and timing can indicate how well auditory development is progressing and are linked with later auditory and language outcomes.",
